        "tree_id": "271387b543a0bbe819839de3a0c777f3cfe59fd9",
        "message": "feat: split TLS ClientHello to bypass Alibaba HZ small-packet RST\n\nAlibaba Cloud Hangzhou entrypoint RSTs TLS handshakes whose ClientHello\nfits in a single TCP segment under ~1441 bytes (only for *.sepic.space).\nAndroid Conscrypt emits ~300-500B ClientHello, so Immich app gets\n'Server is not reachable' while Chrome (BoringSSL, ~1500B) works fine.\n\nWrap SSLSocketFactory and split the first write into 1 + N bytes.\nVerified: single 197B CH -> RST; 1B + 196B -> ServerHello.",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-01T12:19:57Z",
        "author": {
          "name": "240xu",
          "email": "240xu@users.noreply.github.com"
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "240xu",
          "email": "240xu@users.noreply.github.com"
        }
      },
